      "updated": 1755300000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Risks & mitigations",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Risks & mitigations",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "panelbody-0276",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12.0,
      "y": 1486.5,
      "width": 732.6,
      "height": 525.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "g-note-0273"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1241730678,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1859264192,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1755300000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• Karan is two of the five tracks. Integration & Release and Pilot & Consent are the same human, time-sliced,\n  not parallel — that is the week's real ceiling. Mitigation: three agent worktrees is the maximum that stays\n  mergeable, operator work is capped at roughly two hours a day, and Day 1 is deliberately an evening because\n  the scaffold already landed today.\n• Five branches and no integration owner is the most probable way this week actually fails. Mitigation: Karan\n  merges every worktree to main nightly and typecheck + lint + jest must be green before anyone sleeps. The\n  README already declares that bar; from Day 2 it is a scheduled ritual, not a hope.\n• TestFlight external beta review is 24-48h and can bounce, sitting between Wednesday and Friday. Mitigation:\n  submit Wednesday morning, collect the club device UDID on Monday via eas device:create, and cut the ad-hoc\n  build in the same Wednesday batch so the fallback exists as a binary rather than a sentence.\n• The safeguarding officer has a veto and is the likeliest single cause of Friday collapsing. Mitigation: the\n  filming and consent policy is drafted Day 2 and their written sign-off is a Day 3 booking condition — if it\n  is not in hand Monday, the pilot moves rather than proceeds on assumption.\n• The club cancels, or the pro is away. Mitigation: the primary is a club Karan already has a relationship\n  with, a second club is held from the Day 1 email, and Thursday re-confirms. The fallback must still put a\n  club coach on a club-owned device or the demo gate is not met — a public-court session with a member does not\n  count.\n• The simulator has no camera and Karan's iPhone is the only test device, so every capture bug is\n  hardware-only. Mitigation: first real device run is Day 2 at the court, the dev-client build lands Day 3, and\n  the genuine 45-minute endurance take is Day 5 — never a two-minute proxy.\n• Operator gates block all four agent tracks: eas init, the ASC app record, the Apple Team ID and the Azure\n  subscription. Mitigation: all of them are Day 1 evening, before anything downstream needs them; eas.json's\n  TODO_OPERATOR_* placeholders are the literal checklist.\n• Azure is CPU-only this week by design. New subscriptions carry zero GPU quota, a quota increase is a 1-3\n  business-day support ticket, and startup-credit subscriptions are frequently barred from GPU SKUs entirely.\n  Mitigation: audio-onset segmentation needs no GPU, so the week needs only Blob storage and a B-series VM or\n  Function. File the quota request Day 1 anyway so week 2 is not blocked.\n• Storage and interruptions. HEVC at ~6 Mbps is ~2 GB for 45 minutes; iOS suspends AVCaptureSession when the\n  app backgrounds and there is no expo-camera flag that prevents it. Mitigation: chunked capture caps an\n  interruption at one chunk, plus a free-space guard via Paths.availableDiskSpace and Do Not Disturb on the\n  laminated one-pager.\n• Squash is hostile to computer vision — a black 40 mm ball, glass reflections, heavy occlusion. Mitigation:\n  the week-1 target is rally segmentation from audio onsets scored on three hand-labelled clips, not ball\n  tracking and not score inference. Club box-league drives run roughly 100-160 km/h, not the ~270 km/h\n  professional figure both source documents were quoting.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "• Karan is two of the five tracks. Integration & Release and Pilot & Consent are the same human, time-sliced,\n  not parallel — that is the week's real ceiling. Mitigation: three agent worktrees is the maximum that stays\n  mergeable, operator work is capped at roughly two hours a day, and Day 1 is deliberately an evening because\n  the scaffold already landed today.\n• Five branches and no integration owner is the most probable way this week actually fails. Mitigation: Karan\n  merges every worktree to main nightly and typecheck + lint + jest must be green before anyone sleeps. The\n  README already declares that bar; from Day 2 it is a scheduled ritual, not a hope.\n• TestFlight external beta review is 24-48h and can bounce, sitting between Wednesday and Friday. Mitigation:\n  submit Wednesday morning, collect the club device UDID on Monday via eas device:create, and cut the ad-hoc\n  build in the same Wednesday batch so the fallback exists as a binary rather than a sentence.\n• The safeguarding officer has a veto and is the likeliest single cause of Friday collapsing. Mitigation: the\n  filming and consent policy is drafted Day 2 and their written sign-off is a Day 3 booking condition — if it\n  is not in hand Monday, the pilot moves rather than proceeds on assumption.\n• The club cancels, or the pro is away. Mitigation: the primary is a club Karan already has a relationship\n  with, a second club is held from the Day 1 email, and Thursday re-confirms. The fallback must still put a\n  club coach on a club-owned device or the demo gate is not met — a public-court session with a member does not\n  count.\n• The simulator has no camera and Karan's iPhone is the only test device, so every capture bug is\n  hardware-only. Mitigation: first real device run is Day 2 at the court, the dev-client build lands Day 3, and\n  the genuine 45-minute endurance take is Day 5 — never a two-minute proxy.\n• Operator gates block all four agent tracks: eas init, the ASC app record, the Apple Team ID and the Azure\n  subscription. Mitigation: all of them are Day 1 evening, before anything downstream needs them; eas.json's\n  TODO_OPERATOR_* placeholders are the literal checklist.\n• Azure is CPU-only this week by design. New subscriptions carry zero GPU quota, a quota increase is a 1-3\n  business-day support ticket, and startup-credit subscriptions are frequently barred from GPU SKUs entirely.\n  Mitigation: audio-onset segmentation needs no GPU, so the week needs only Blob storage and a B-series VM or\n  Function. File the quota request Day 1 anyway so week 2 is not blocked.\n• Storage and interruptions. HEVC at ~6 Mbps is ~2 GB for 45 minutes; iOS suspends AVCaptureSession when the\n  app backgrounds and there is no expo-camera flag that prevents it. Mitigation: chunked capture caps an\n  interruption at one chunk, plus a free-space guard via Paths.availableDiskSpace and Do Not Disturb on the\n  laminated one-pager.\n• Squash is hostile to computer vision — a black 40 mm ball, glass reflections, heavy occlusion. Mitigation:\n  the week-1 target is rally segmentation from audio onsets scored on three hand-labelled clips, not ball\n  tracking and not score inference. Club box-league drives run roughly 100-160 km/h, not the ~270 km/h\n  professional figure both source documents were quoting.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
