    {
      "id": "panelbody-0280",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 789.67,
      "y": 1486.5,
      "width": 732.6,
      "height": 270.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "g-note-0277"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1563921604,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 64228086,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1755300000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• No AI inference inside the app, real-time or otherwise. Every AI step runs offline on already-recorded video,\n  and Day 3's framing overlay is drawn by hand and eyeballed by the operator — no line detection, no\n  homography, no calibration.\n• No Score AI tab in v0.1.0. A permanently empty tab is a standard App Review 2.1 placeholder rejection, so the\n  route ships behind a dev flag and the app is described to review as exactly what it is: a match recorder.\n• No automatic scoring of any kind. The manual PAR-11 tap scoreboard does ship — squash.ts is already a tested\n  pure reducer on main — but the AI that would fill it does not.\n• No accounts, no backend, no upload from the app. Footage stays on device and Azure gets files hand-carried\n  off it, which is also why there is no share link this week.\n• No Photos-library write until deletion works end to end. A copy in someone's camera roll cannot be recalled,\n  and the deletion path lands the same day as the export.\n• Canada only for this pilot's legal work — one jurisdiction, Milton being the operating base. UK and US\n  paperwork is market entry, not week one. Note the source requirement had it backwards: UK GDPR is the\n  stricter bar, not PIPEDA.\n• No Android, no App Store submission, no payments or pricing conversation. TestFlight only, and the pilot is\n  free.\n• No booking, league, ladder or ratings integration. Club Locker and SportyHQ own that rail and neither has a\n  confirmed write API.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "• No AI inference inside the app, real-time or otherwise. Every AI step runs offline on already-recorded video,\n  and Day 3's framing overlay is drawn by hand and eyeballed by the operator — no line detection, no\n  homography, no calibration.\n• No Score AI tab in v0.1.0. A permanently empty tab is a standard App Review 2.1 placeholder rejection, so the\n  route ships behind a dev flag and the app is described to review as exactly what it is: a match recorder.\n• No automatic scoring of any kind. The manual PAR-11 tap scoreboard does ship — squash.ts is already a tested\n  pure reducer on main — but the AI that would fill it does not.\n• No accounts, no backend, no upload from the app. Footage stays on device and Azure gets files hand-carried\n  off it, which is also why there is no share link this week.\n• No Photos-library write until deletion works end to end. A copy in someone's camera roll cannot be recalled,\n  and the deletion path lands the same day as the export.\n• Canada only for this pilot's legal work — one jurisdiction, Milton being the operating base. UK and US\n  paperwork is market entry, not week one. Note the source requirement had it backwards: UK GDPR is the\n  stricter bar, not PIPEDA.\n• No Android, no App Store submission, no payments or pricing conversation. TestFlight only, and the pilot is\n  free.\n• No booking, league, ladder or ratings integration. Club Locker and SportyHQ own that rail and neither has a\n  confirmed write API.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
