      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1755300000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• A club coach, on a club-owned device, installs RacquetAI from TestFlight and records a full box-league match\n  — 30-50 minutes of best-of-5 PAR-11, not a 20-minute blowout — in landscape from the gallery.\n• That recording plays back full length in Library on the same device with the session sheet attached: both\n  players, court number, sport and best-of.\n• Nobody in the room walked away thinking the app scores matches. The one-page brief says so in writing and\n  there is no Score AI tab to imply otherwise.\n• The match file comes off the club phone inside the 20 minutes budgeted for it, runs through the CPU-only\n  Azure runner, and returns a rally timeline within ±2 rallies of a hand count — replayed lets counted as\n  separate rallies, with the hand-counter logging lets separately so the comparison is apples to apples.\n• Deleting that match on the device removes the video, its sidecar and every derived clip — demonstrated in\n  front of the coach, not asserted.\n• main is green — typecheck, lint and jest — at the v0.1.0 tag the club is holding.\n• Karan leaves with a written next step from the club: a second session booked, or an explicit no with the\n  reason.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "• A club coach, on a club-owned device, installs RacquetAI from TestFlight and records a full box-league match\n  — 30-50 minutes of best-of-5 PAR-11, not a 20-minute blowout — in landscape from the gallery.\n• That recording plays back full length in Library on the same device with the session sheet attached: both\n  players, court number, sport and best-of.\n• Nobody in the room walked away thinking the app scores matches. The one-page brief says so in writing and\n  there is no Score AI tab to imply otherwise.\n• The match file comes off the club phone inside the 20 minutes budgeted for it, runs through the CPU-only\n  Azure runner, and returns a rally timeline within ±2 rallies of a hand count — replayed lets counted as\n  separate rallies, with the hand-counter logging lets separately so the comparison is apples to apples.\n• Deleting that match on the device removes the video, its sidecar and every derived clip — demonstrated in\n  front of the coach, not asserted.\n• main is green — typecheck, lint and jest — at the v0.1.0 tag the club is holding.\n• Karan leaves with a written next step from the club: a second session booked, or an explicit no with the\n  reason.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
