      "updated": 1755300000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• Confirm what the pilot club actually runs before writing any connector, and\n  order the list by the pilot's country. For Ontario the two candidates are\n  SportyHQ and Club Locker, and the research is contradictory — Squash Canada\n  selected Club Locker in 2018 and Ontario adopted it, yet SportyHQ is also\n  described as dominant among Canadian clubs. One phone call settles it. ClubSpark\n  is LTA/tennis-centric and does not belong at the top of a squash list; the\n  realistic UK squash stack is SportyHQ, Club Locker, myClubhouse or Sport80, and\n  that is market-entry, not the pilot.\n• CSV in and CSV out is the P0 integration; every API is P1 because none of them\n  is signed. Club Locker exposes api.ussquash.com but has no public docs, endpoint\n  list, auth model or partner programme, so assume a commercial conversation with\n  the new majority owner. That owner is reported as Artisan Ventures from November\n  2025 — corroborated by Squash Canada and search snippets, with terms and price\n  unverified — so do not state it flatly in a deck.\n• The ratings payload is tiny: (player A, player B, game scores, point scores,\n  date, event type). USR ingests every match recorded in Club Locker —\n  tournaments, leagues, ladders and friendlies — and updates daily; SquashLevels\n  weights POINT scores, not just game wins, so point-level accuracy is what makes\n  the hook work. No public WRITE API is confirmed for either, and that is the\n  first email to send.\n• Member identity — club SSO or an email-matched directory — so a recorded player\n  maps to a real membership and a real rating. Until that exists, match history\n  stays device-local, which is why the Feedback pillar scopes it that way rather\n  than promising a club-wide archive.\n• Fix the canonical enums now, against World Squash Rules of Singles Squash 2025\n  v1.2 (effective 1 Sept 2025): rally outcomes are winner, error, Yes Let (replay,\n  no point), Stroke and No Let; shot types are drive, drop, boast, lob, kill, nick\n  and volley, plus serve and error. Expect volley, lob and nick to need height\n  information or a user correction.\n• Do not build booking, leagues or ladders. Club Locker, SportyHQ and CourtReserve\n  own that and no club will switch booking systems to get video. The one thing\n  worth importing is the box-league round: self-scheduled, unrefereed,\n  score-disputed, already tracked digitally, and the highest-frequency recordable\n  event in any club.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "• Confirm what the pilot club actually runs before writing any connector, and\n  order the list by the pilot's country. For Ontario the two candidates are\n  SportyHQ and Club Locker, and the research is contradictory — Squash Canada\n  selected Club Locker in 2018 and Ontario adopted it, yet SportyHQ is also\n  described as dominant among Canadian clubs. One phone call settles it. ClubSpark\n  is LTA/tennis-centric and does not belong at the top of a squash list; the\n  realistic UK squash stack is SportyHQ, Club Locker, myClubhouse or Sport80, and\n  that is market-entry, not the pilot.\n• CSV in and CSV out is the P0 integration; every API is P1 because none of them\n  is signed. Club Locker exposes api.ussquash.com but has no public docs, endpoint\n  list, auth model or partner programme, so assume a commercial conversation with\n  the new majority owner. That owner is reported as Artisan Ventures from November\n  2025 — corroborated by Squash Canada and search snippets, with terms and price\n  unverified — so do not state it flatly in a deck.\n• The ratings payload is tiny: (player A, player B, game scores, point scores,\n  date, event type). USR ingests every match recorded in Club Locker —\n  tournaments, leagues, ladders and friendlies — and updates daily; SquashLevels\n  weights POINT scores, not just game wins, so point-level accuracy is what makes\n  the hook work. No public WRITE API is confirmed for either, and that is the\n  first email to send.\n• Member identity — club SSO or an email-matched directory — so a recorded player\n  maps to a real membership and a real rating. Until that exists, match history\n  stays device-local, which is why the Feedback pillar scopes it that way rather\n  than promising a club-wide archive.\n• Fix the canonical enums now, against World Squash Rules of Singles Squash 2025\n  v1.2 (effective 1 Sept 2025): rally outcomes are winner, error, Yes Let (replay,\n  no point), Stroke and No Let; shot types are drive, drop, boast, lob, kill, nick\n  and volley, plus serve and error. Expect volley, lob and nick to need height\n  information or a user correction.\n• Do not build booking, leagues or ladders. Club Locker, SportyHQ and CourtReserve\n  own that and no club will switch booking systems to get video. The one thing\n  worth importing is the box-league round: self-scheduled, unrefereed,\n  score-disputed, already tracked digitally, and the highest-frequency recordable\n  event in any club.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
