    {
      "id": "panelbody-0496",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 595.25,
      "y": 3652.5,
      "width": 541.2,
      "height": 285.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "g-req-0493"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 425935766,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1168381199,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1755300000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• One named owner inside the club, realistically the head pro or the box-league\n  organiser — not the GM and not the front desk.\n• Zero-staff recording is a hard requirement, not a preference. Box matches are\n  self-scheduled at 9pm; anything that needs a person to set it up will simply not\n  happen. That is why the permanent clamp plus a docked, charging phone is P1\n  rather than a later moat — for the pilot Karan mounts it himself, but that\n  configuration is not the product.\n• Someone owns charging, re-mounting and wiping the lens on the phone. Agree whose\n  job that is, in writing, before the pilot starts.\n• A 15-minute onboarding for the pro plus a laminated card at the court door:\n  mount, tap, confirm consent (video and audio), enable Do Not Disturb, play.\n• Three people must be in the first meeting — the GM signs, the pro champions, and\n  the safeguarding officer can veto — and the safeguarding officer's written\n  non-objection to the filming policy must land BEFORE the pilot date is\n  confirmed. That is the likeliest single cause of a pilot collapsing on the day.\n• Support is a direct text thread to Karan during the pilot; an SLA only once it\n  is paid. Budget 20 minutes on pilot day to hand-carry 2–3.5 GB off a club-owned\n  phone with a member standing there, and pre-test that exact transfer on a real\n  match file the day before.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "• One named owner inside the club, realistically the head pro or the box-league\n  organiser — not the GM and not the front desk.\n• Zero-staff recording is a hard requirement, not a preference. Box matches are\n  self-scheduled at 9pm; anything that needs a person to set it up will simply not\n  happen. That is why the permanent clamp plus a docked, charging phone is P1\n  rather than a later moat — for the pilot Karan mounts it himself, but that\n  configuration is not the product.\n• Someone owns charging, re-mounting and wiping the lens on the phone. Agree whose\n  job that is, in writing, before the pilot starts.\n• A 15-minute onboarding for the pro plus a laminated card at the court door:\n  mount, tap, confirm consent (video and audio), enable Do Not Disturb, play.\n• Three people must be in the first meeting — the GM signs, the pro champions, and\n  the safeguarding officer can veto — and the safeguarding officer's written\n  non-objection to the filming policy must land BEFORE the pilot date is\n  confirmed. That is the likeliest single cause of a pilot collapsing on the day.\n• Support is a direct text thread to Karan during the pilot; an SLA only once it\n  is paid. Budget 20 minutes on pilot day to hand-carry 2–3.5 GB off a club-owned\n  phone with a member standing there, and pre-test that exact transfer on a real\n  match file the day before.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
