    {
      "id": "panelbody-0504",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12.0,
      "y": 4245.0,
      "width": 1960.2,
      "height": 90.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "g-oq-0501"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1048633225,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 969744766,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1755300000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "? Does your back wall have full glass, and may I clamp a phone about two metres behind it, in a corner of the glass? Full-glass back walls are a minority of club courts and this is the hardest filter on the whole target list — ask it in the first thirty seconds of the call, not on the site visit.\n? Which system do you run the box league on — SportyHQ, Club Locker, something else — and can you export this month's boxes as a CSV? That answer decides the first integration and whether a recorded match arrives already knowing both players and the round.\n? If it took one tap, what share of your monthly box matches would actually get recorded — 10%, 50% or 90%? Below roughly 30% the club dashboard has no data in it and the ratings hook is noise.\n? Who owns footage of a member's match at your club — the club, the player or the coach — and has anything in your terms ever answered that? No precedent was found anywhere, and it blocks both the pilot notice and the first contract.\n? What would stop your junior box league being filmed, and does a written filming policy plus per-session parent consent clear it with your safeguarding officer? Juniors are where clubs film most, so if this fails the highest-volume use case is off the table.\n? What line item would this come out of and what is its ceiling — a $25/mo software add-on, a per-member fee, or the coaching P&L? That single number decides per-court versus per-player pricing.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "? Does your back wall have full glass, and may I clamp a phone about two metres behind it, in a corner of the glass? Full-glass back walls are a minority of club courts and this is the hardest filter on the whole target list — ask it in the first thirty seconds of the call, not on the site visit.\n? Which system do you run the box league on — SportyHQ, Club Locker, something else — and can you export this month's boxes as a CSV? That answer decides the first integration and whether a recorded match arrives already knowing both players and the round.\n? If it took one tap, what share of your monthly box matches would actually get recorded — 10%, 50% or 90%? Below roughly 30% the club dashboard has no data in it and the ratings hook is noise.\n? Who owns footage of a member's match at your club — the club, the player or the coach — and has anything in your terms ever answered that? No precedent was found anywhere, and it blocks both the pilot notice and the first contract.\n? What would stop your junior box league being filmed, and does a written filming policy plus per-session parent consent clear it with your safeguarding officer? Juniors are where clubs film most, so if this fails the highest-volume use case is off the table.\n? What line item would this come out of and what is its ceiling — a $25/mo software add-on, a per-member fee, or the coaching P&L? That single number decides per-court versus per-player pricing.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    }
